  "worked_solution": "First, we factor out the constants and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4a\\cdot (-b\\times c) & =12 \\\\ 4\\cdot (-1)\\cdot [a\\cdot (b\\times c)] & =12 \\\\ a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $a$ and $b$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\cdot (a\\times c) & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
